---
const posts = [
  {
    id: "sql-locks",
    title: "Resolving Concurrent Blocking in SQL Server and Softland Exactus ERP",
    category: "sysadmin",
    categoryName: "Enterprise Infrastructure & Databases",
    date: "Jun 12, 2026",
    readTime: "6 min read",
    summary: "Engineering deep dive into diagnosing and resolving high-concurrency transactional bottlenecks, deadlocks, and blocking chains in SQL Server databases supporting enterprise ERP systems.",
    content: `
      <p>One of the most frequent challenges in enterprise database administration is resource locking. In infrastructures running Enterprise Resource Planning software (such as the Softland Exactus ERP operating on Microsoft SQL Server), high concurrency can rapidly degrade performance if left unmanaged.</p>
      
      <h4>Root Cause of the Problem</h4>
      <p>When multiple users or background batch processes attempt to update identical tables simultaneously (such as during bulk invoicing runs or end-of-month accounting closures), SQL Server utilizes locks to protect data integrity and isolation. However, when an unoptimized query holds exclusive locks for too long, a blocking chain cascades across the instance, stalling downstream user operations.</p>
      
      <h4>Real-Time Diagnosis & Live Troubleshooting</h4>
      <p>To pinpoint the lead blocking session and culprit SQL query, we deploy audit scripts leveraging SQL Server Dynamic Management Views (DMVs). The core live diagnostic query is:</p>
      
      <pre><code>SELECT 
    blocking_session_id AS BlockingSessionID,
    session_id AS BlockedSessionID,
    wait_type AS WaitType,
    wait_time / 1000 AS WaitTimeSeconds,
    (SELECT text FROM sys.dm_exec_sql_text(sql_handle)) AS QueryText
FROM sys.dm_exec_requests
WHERE blocking_session_id <> 0;</code></pre>

      <h4>Mitigation Strategies & Best Practices</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Index Optimization:</strong> Analyze query execution plans to identify missing non-clustered indexes, accelerating lookup speeds and shortening shared/exclusive lock durations.</li>
        <li><strong>Read Committed Snapshot Isolation (RCSI):</strong> Evaluate enabling RCSI on the database instance, allowing readers to access versioned snapshot data without blocking concurrent writers.</li>
        <li><strong>Proactive Alerting:</strong> Configure automated SQL Server Agent alerts to notify the SysAdmin team immediately whenever aggregate blocking duration exceeds 30 seconds.</li>
      </ul>
    `
  },
  {
    id: "entra-pim",
    title: "Hardening Access Control: Implementing Microsoft Entra PIM and Conditional Access MFA",
    category: "devsecops",
    categoryName: "Cybersecurity & DevSecOps",
    date: "May 28, 2026",
    readTime: "8 min read",
    summary: "Step-by-step configuration of Privileged Identity Management (PIM) to enforce Just-In-Time administrative access combined with Conditional Access MFA policies.",
    content: `
      <p>In modern cloud and hybrid IT security architectures, granting permanent standing privileges is an unacceptable operational risk. The principle of least privilege mandates that administrative roles be granted strictly on-demand, for a predetermined duration, and under rigorous verification.</p>
      
      <h4>What is Microsoft Entra PIM?</h4>
      <p>Privileged Identity Management (PIM) mitigates credential compromise risk by replacing persistent elevated rights with "eligible roles". When administrators need to execute high-impact configuration tasks, they must actively initiate a time-bounded role elevation session subject to security guardrails.</p>
      
      <h4>Enforcing Zero Trust Security Policies</h4>
      <p>Our recommended governance blueprint for securing directory tenants encompasses four key pillars:</p>
      
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Mandatory Conditional Access MFA:</strong> Prior to requesting role activation, the user must satisfy phishing-resistant multifactor authentication challenges.</li>
        <li><strong>Peer Approval Workflows:</strong> Critical roles (such as Global Administrator, Privileged Role Admin, or Exchange Admin) require explicit dual-authorization from another senior infrastructure lead.</li>
        <li><strong>Business Justification & Ticket Binding:</strong> Every activation requires a documented operational reason and a valid support ticket ID (ServiceNow/Jira).</li>
        <li><strong>Automated Access Reviews:</strong> Scheduled weekly auditing reports capturing elevation logs, role usage frequency, and post-activity review histories to ensure pristine forensic posture.</li>
      </ol>
      
      <p>This implementation reduces the attack surface of the Entra ID tenant by over 80%, ensuring zero standing administrative privileges exist unmonitored or outside active operational windows.</p>
    `
  },
  {
    id: "chess-sysadmin",
    title: "Chess and Systems Administration: What the Board Teaches About Managing Infrastructure",
    category: "offduty",
    categoryName: "Off the Terminal",
    date: "May 10, 2026",
    readTime: "5 min read",
    summary: "Connecting chess strategy, positional control, and foresight with incident response and resilient engineering in IT and DevSecOps.",
    content: `
      <p>At first glance, a fleet of Linux servers orchestrated in the cloud and a sixty-four square chessboard share little in common. Yet, my regular chess practice has revealed profound philosophical and practical parallels to systems administration.</p>
      
      <h4>1. Center Control and Critical Infrastructure</h4>
      <p>In chess, dominating the central squares (d4, d5, e4, e5) determines tempo and spatial control. In network operations, the center represents your mission-critical backbone: primary database clusters, default gateways configured with HSRP redundancy, and centralized identity providers (Entra ID). If you neglect hardening or monitoring these core assets, your entire positional perimeter collapses.</p>
      
      <h4>2. Tactics vs. Strategy (Firefighting vs. Automation)</h4>
      <p>A novice player moves reactively, responding to the opponent's immediate move without a long-term plan. This mirrors the SysAdmin trapped in eternal firefighting—spending whole days resolving manual tickets. Chess instills strategic thinking: formulating structural architectural improvements (such as IaC and automated CI/CD pipelines) while adeptly navigating immediate operational constraints.</p>
      
      <h4>3. The Post-Mortem Blunder Analysis</h4>
      <p>The single most reliable method for improving at chess is conducting thorough post-game reviews to uncover the root blunder that caused a loss. In DevSecOps, this is identical to blameless post-mortem incident analyses. When an outage occurs, restoring service is only half the battle; the true engineering value lies in interrogating telemetry logs to systematically eliminate that vulnerability forever.</p>
    `
  }
];
---

<section id="blog" class="blog-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Technical Blog & Insights</h2>
    
    <div class="blog-grid">
      {posts.map(post => (
        <article class="blog-card glass-card" data-post-id={post.id}>
          <div class="blog-meta">
            <span class={`blog-category cat-${post.category}`}>{post.categoryName}</span>
            <span class="blog-date">{post.date}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="blog-title">{post.title}</h3>
          <p class="blog-summary">{post.summary}</p>
          <div class="blog-footer">
            <span class="read-time">{post.readTime}</span>
            <button class="read-btn" data-post-id={post.id}>
              Read Article 
              <span class="arrow">→</span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Dynamic Modal Reader -->
  <div class="blog-modal" id="blogModal" aria-hidden="true" role="dialog">
    <div class="modal-backdrop"></div>
    <div class="modal-wrapper">
      <div class="modal-content glass-card">
        <div class="modal-header">
          <div class="modal-meta-row">
            <span class="modal-category" id="modalCategory">Category</span>
            <span class="modal-date" id="modalDate">Date</span>
            <span class="modal-readtime" id="modalReadTime">Read Time</span>
          </div>
          <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close article">✕</button>
        </div>
        <div class="modal-body-scroll">
          <h3 class="modal-title" id="modalTitle">Article Title</h3>
          <div class="modal-divider"></div>
          <div class="modal-body" id="modalBody">
            Loading content...
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .blog-section {
    padding: 100px 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .blog-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(350px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .blog-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .blog-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .blog-category {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .cat-sysadmin {
    background: rgba(0, 255, 136, 0.08);
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 255, 136, 0.2);
  }

  .cat-devsecops {
    background: rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.08);
    color: #00D2FF;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.2);
  }

  .cat-offduty {
    background: rgba(157, 78, 221, 0.08);
    color: #9D4EDD;
    border: 1px solid rgba(157, 78, 221, 0.2);
  }

  .blog-date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .blog-title {
    font-family: var(--font-title);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    flex-grow: 0;
  }

  .blog-summary {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .blog-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .read-time {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .read-btn {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .read-btn .arrow {
    transition: var(--transition-smooth);
  }

  .blog-card:hover .read-btn .arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  /* Modal Reader Styles */
  .blog-modal {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    z-index: 150;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .blog-modal.open {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .modal-backdrop {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: rgba(4, 6, 10, 0.85);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  }

  .modal-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    width: 90%;
    max-width: 750px;
    max-height: 85vh;
    z-index: 10;
    transform: scale(0.95) translateY(20px);
    transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .blog-modal.open .modal-wrapper {
    transform: scale(1) translateY(0);
  }

  .modal-content {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-height: 85vh;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .modal-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  .modal-meta-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .modal-category {
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .modal-date {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .modal-readtime {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .modal-close {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .modal-close:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  .modal-body-scroll {
    padding: 2rem 2.5rem 3rem 2.5rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }

  .modal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-title);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .modal-divider {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border-color);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .modal-body {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .modal-body h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-title);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .modal-body pre {
    background: #05070A;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .modal-body ul, .modal-body ol {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .modal-body ul { list-style: disc; }
  .modal-body ol { list-style: decimal; }

  .modal-body strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .blog-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .modal-body-scroll {
      padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 2.5rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .modal-title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .modal-header {
      padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .modal-meta-row {
      gap: 0.75rem;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script define:vars={{ posts }}>
  // Modal handling logic
  const modal = document.getElementById('blogModal');
  const backdrop = modal.querySelector('.modal-backdrop');
  const closeBtn = modal.querySelector('.modal-close');
  const modalCategory = document.getElementById('modalCategory');
  const modalDate = document.getElementById('modalDate');
  const modalReadTime = document.getElementById('modalReadTime');
  const modalTitle = document.getElementById('modalTitle');
  const modalBody = document.getElementById('modalBody');

  function openArticle(postId) {
    const post = posts.find(p => p.id === postId);
    if (!post || !modal) return;

    // Populate Modal Content
    if (modalCategory) {
      modalCategory.textContent = post.categoryName;
      modalCategory.className = `modal-category cat-${post.category}`;
    }
    if (modalDate) modalDate.textContent = post.date;
    if (modalReadTime) modalReadTime.textContent = post.readTime;
    if (modalTitle) modalTitle.textContent = post.title;
    if (modalBody) modalBody.innerHTML = post.content;

    // Show Modal
    modal.classList.add('open');
    modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden'; // Lock background scroll
  }

  function closeArticle() {
    if (!modal) return;
    modal.classList.remove('open');
    modal.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
    document.body.style.overflow = ''; // Unlock background scroll
  }

  // Click handler for blog cards
  document.querySelectorAll('.blog-card').forEach(card => {
    card.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const postId = card.getAttribute('data-post-id');
      if (postId) openArticle(postId);
    });
  });

  // Click handlers for close buttons & backdrop
  closeBtn?.addEventListener('click', closeArticle);
  backdrop?.addEventListener('click', closeArticle);

  // Close modal on escape key
  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && modal?.classList.contains('open')) {
      closeArticle();
    }
  });
</script>
